    "scenario": "MPLS TTL Propagation Control",
    "goals": "• {{router1_name}} is a customer router attached to the provider edge {{router2_name}} over {{link1_cidr}}. OSPF area 0 and the Loopback0 addresses are already configured on all four routers, so every router can reach every Loopback0 over plain IP.\n• {{router2_name}}, {{router3_name}} and {{router4_name}} form the provider core, and MPLS forwarding with LDP is already enabled and operational on the two core links {{link2_cidr}} and {{link3_cidr}} only. The access link {{link1_cidr}} towards {{router1_name}} carries no MPLS.\n    customer: {{router1_name}}\n    MPLS core: {{router2_name}}, {{router3_name}}, {{router4_name}}\n• A traceroute launched from {{router1_name}} towards {{router4_name}} Loopback0 ({{router4_loopback0_ip}}) currently exposes every core router hop by hop, because the IP TTL is copied into the label header.\n• Hide the core from customer traceroutes: on the core routers, stop copying the IP TTL into the label header for transit traffic that the router forwards, so the whole label switched path is reported as a single hop.\n• Traffic that a core router originates itself must keep normal TTL handling, and end-to-end reachability from {{router1_name}} to {{router4_loopback0_ip}} must not change.",
    "topology_model": {
        "nodes": [
            "r1",
            "r2",
            "r3",
            "r4"
        ],
        "links": [
            {
                "id": "link1",
                "nodes": [
